<figure class="art-fig">
<svg viewBox="0 0 640 534" role="img" aria-label="How a synthetic identity turns into a loss" aria-describedby="f2-d" font-family="inherit">
<title id="f2-t">How a synthetic identity turns into a loss</title>
<desc id="f2-d">Four stages. One: build the identity from real and invented data by fabrication, manipulation or compilation; data checks at onboarding can catch it. Two: get a credit file, which even a rejected application can create. Three: build a history with on-time payments, sometimes as an authorized user on a good account. Four: bust-out, when every credit line is maxed out and payments stop. Stages two to four are visible only through account monitoring.</desc>
<path d="M48 40 L48 424" stroke="var(--line-strong)" stroke-width="3"/><circle cx="48" cy="40" r="22" fill="var(--accent)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="48" y="46" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="var(--surface)">1</text><text x="92" y="46" font-size="19" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Build the identity</text><text x="92" y="72" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">Real and invented data combined:</text><text x="92" y="92" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">fabrication, manipulation or compilation</text><rect x="92" y="104" width="328" height="26" rx="13" fill="var(--accent-soft)"/><text x="104" y="122" font-size="13" fill="var(--accent)" font-weight="600">Where to look: data checks at onboarding</text><circle cx="48" cy="168" r="22" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="48" y="174" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">2</text><text x="92" y="174" font-size="19" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Get a credit file</text><text x="92" y="200" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">Even a rejected application can</text><text x="92" y="220" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">create a file for the new identity</text><rect x="92" y="232" width="275" height="26" rx="13" fill="var(--accent-soft)"/><text x="104" y="250" font-size="13" fill="var(--accent)" font-weight="600">Where to look: account monitoring</text><circle cx="48" cy="296" r="22" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="48" y="302" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">3</text><text x="92" y="302" font-size="19" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Build a history</text><text x="92" y="328" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">On-time payments; sometimes added</text><text x="92" y="348" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">as an authorized user on a good account</text><rect x="92" y="360" width="275" height="26" rx="13" fill="var(--accent-soft)"/><text x="104" y="378" font-size="13" fill="var(--accent)" font-weight="600">Where to look: account monitoring</text><circle cx="48" cy="424" r="22" fill="var(--accent)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="48" y="430" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="var(--surface)">4</text><text x="92" y="430" font-size="19" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">Bust-out</text><text x="92" y="456" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">Every credit line is maxed out, then</text><text x="92" y="476" font-size="15" fill="var(--body)">payments stop; no real person to pursue</text><rect x="92" y="488" width="275" height="26" rx="13" fill="var(--accent-soft)"/><text x="104" y="506" font-size="13" fill="var(--accent)" font-weight="600">Where to look: account monitoring</text>
</svg>
<figcaption>Based on the Federal Reserve's description of synthetic identity fraud. Only the first stage happens at onboarding.</figcaption>
</figure>
